          "kicker": "Club travel scare",
          "heading": "France winger Bielle-Biarrey stranded at Bristol Airport with Bordeaux Bègles teammates",
          "body": "France winger Louis Bielle-Biarrey was one of four Bordeaux Bègles players temporarily denied entry to the UK, stranded at Bristol Airport with loose forward Romain Gardrat, loosehead Matis Perchaud and Tonga prop Toma Taufa, plus a fitness coach. A club source told AFP the group lacked valid Electronic Travel Authorisation permits, their approvals linked to passports renewed earlier this year. The issue was resolved through the French embassy in London, and the players rejoined the squad before Bordeaux's Champions Cup opener against Gloucester."
