          "heading": "Scotland women face the Wallaroos again in Canberra after Sydney rout",
          "body": "Scotland women face the Wallaroos again on Friday in Canberra, after an eight-try 56-12 defeat in Sydney on Saturday. Katie Buchanan gave them a fifth-minute lead and captain Rachel Malcolm also crossed, but Australia scored five tries before half-time and Desiree Miller became the first Wallaroo to reach 20 Test tries. Caretaker coach Dave Butcher also had to replace Sarah Bonar, lost to illness shortly before kick-off, with Hollie Cunningham."
