          "heading": "Dafydd Jenkins says Welsh players moving to Prem can strengthen regions",
          "body": "Dafydd Jenkins believes the flood of Welsh talent heading to the English Prem will benefit the home game. The Exeter lock, 23, who has spent all his senior career at Sandy Park, says the move opens space for the next generation. \"I think the positive in that is that they're opening up space for another young hooker, another young back-rower,\" he told BBC Sport. Captain Jac Morgan and Dewi Lake joined Gloucester from the Ospreys this summer, and Jenkins has started all three of Exeter's league matches this season."
